{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NFcUJov1j8uim9AfgvMPJE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# stories-api\n2\t\n3\tA small story library behind `POST /stories` (Lambda + DynamoDB table `stories`,\n4\tpartition key `slug`). `src/app.py` is the whole service: `handler()` parses\n5\tthe request and `publish()` stores the story together with its three most\n6\tsimilar existing stories (`similar: [{slug, score}]`), so the reader page can\n7\tshow \"related\" without any query at read time. `logs/error.log` is the\n8\tproduction log from the first two publishes after the deploy.\n9\t\n10\tTests use an in-memory table (`tests/fake_dynamo.py`) that validates items the\n11\tway boto3 does, so no AWS account is needed. Run them with\n12\t`python3 -m unittest discover tests` from the repo root.\n13\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0eefa4d0-c24c-43bd-97f8-2ea4e7462032","uuid":"836d50ad-33bd-4327-ad6c-42d80c4a2e25","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:29:29.717Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-UDTqXK/README.md","content":"# stories-api\n\nA small story library behind `POST /stories` (Lambda + DynamoDB table `stories`,\npartition key `slug`). `src/app.py` is the whole service: `handler()` parses\nthe request and `publish()` stores the story together with its three most\nsimilar existing stories (`similar: [{slug, score}]`), so the reader page can\nshow \"related\" without any query at read time. `logs/error.log` is the\nproduction log from the first two publishes after the deploy.\n\nTests use an in-memory table (`tests/fake_dynamo.py`) that validates items the\nway boto3 does, so no AWS account is needed. Run them with\n`python3 -m unittest discover tests` from the repo root.\n","numLines":13,"startLine":1,"totalLines":13}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NFcUJov1j8uim9AfgvMPJE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
